ould discover  a planet you know around another star in  our milky way that was  obviously people absolutely loved that  and  there did end up being someone who had  discovered a planet that like computer  algorithms he missed in the data  and he was a guy from the northeast of  england retired guy  and the media descended on his house  right and we're like  why did you get involved in this like  incredible project like what was it was  it the discovery that like  drove you to to do this and he was like  well there's only so much gardening you  can do and there's just not a lot on  telly lately  just this retired guy and they're like  do you think you you've caught the bug  do you want to catch another one he's  like no probably not i'll probably do  something different  to know that what i was spending my time  doing was  useful to someone somewhere whether it  was you know classifying the shapes of  galaxies or  the shapes of craters on mars or  flagging where there are penguins and  images from antarctica  those huge raft of different cities and  science projects  and it's it's yeah it's a tool to get  people into it but it's also a tool to  let them be involved in science  themselves  when i finished my university undergrad  i was like  so lost of what to do right i loved  school  and i felt bereft when i left school  right and so when i got to university i  was like few four years at least now i  like this this  is fine and then the end of that four  years i was like bereft again not  knowing what to do because  i just love learning and that and just  these halls of learning i was like i  want to do this for the rest of my life  and i didn't realize at the time that  going into research meant you will still  be learning for the rest of your life  right because you're not necessarily  being taught it anymore you're the one  figuring out the answers you know no  one's telling you the answers anymore  you're  literally like writing the textbooks  it's not like solving harder homework  problems right  exactly it's problems that might not  have an answer i mean you didn't know if  you'd finally answer these questions  quenching questions  until you actually did it

